# JetBrains IDEs (GoLand / IntelliJ IDEA).
# User-specific IDE state is ignored; the shared run configurations under
# .idea/runConfigurations/ ARE tracked, so everyone gets the correct build tags
# and GOTMPDIR without rediscovering them. See kanz/docs/jetbrains-setup.md.
.idea/*
!.idea/runConfigurations/
*.iml

# Project-local Go temp dir. Windows Application Control intermittently blocks
# freshly built test binaries in %TEMP%, so the Makefile and the shared run
# configurations point GOTMPDIR here instead.
.gotmp/

# Stripped release binaries (`make release`).
bin/

# Binaries left in-tree by a bare `go build ./cmd/...`, which writes the
# executable into the working directory rather than bin/. Named explicitly per
# command rather than as a blanket rule: `kanz` and `operator` are also directory
# names in this repo, and a pattern broad enough to catch the binaries would
# silently ignore the source trees beside them.
/kanz/universe
/kanz/universe.exe
/kanz/kanz-provisioner
/kanz/kanz-provisioner.exe
